        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e09c62b7-484c-5765-8f2c-575838ba3f1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl\n- People: Mohamed Sanu\n- Organizations: Rutgers Scarlet Knights, UCF, Atlanta Falcons, National Football League\n- Places: Tropicana Field, St. Petersburg, Florida\n- Topics: college football bowl games, Big East\n\nFacts:\n- The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl presented by Beef 'O' Brady's was the second edition of the college football bowl game and was played at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Florida.\n- Rutgers defeated UCF 45–24 in the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl.\n- Mohamed Sanu was the MVP of the 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl after catching 4 passes for 97 yards and a touchdown and rushing 14 times for 47 yards and two touchdowns.\n- The 2009 Rutgers Scarlet Knights football team finished the season 9–4, went 3–4 in Big East play, and won the St. Petersburg Bowl 45–24 over UCF.\n- Mohamed Sanu Sr., born August 22, 1989, is an American football wide receiver for the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
